interviewing others.

00:50:57.370 --> 00:51:00.730
- Yeah, so I had a
few opening roles

00:51:02.260 --> 00:51:04.240
a few months ago at Microsoft

00:51:06.160 --> 00:51:10.180
to work with AI. So
two, I think, hot things. Like,

00:51:10.180 --> 00:51:11.500
working for Microsoft and AI.

00:51:12.460 --> 00:51:13.495
Especially because Microsoft

00:51:14.350 --> 00:51:15.775
is doing well right now.

00:51:17.800 --> 00:51:21.670
So it was a little
chaotic because one,

00:51:22.660 --> 00:51:25.195
people would reach
out to me every day

00:51:25.940 --> 00:51:27.730
to learn more about the role.

00:51:30.190 --> 00:51:33.520
And I think the reason why
also a lot of people were reaching

00:51:33.520 --> 00:51:35.800
out to me, not only
because Microsoft and AI,

00:51:35.800 --> 00:51:39.100
it's because we went
through massive layoffs

00:51:39.880 --> 00:51:41.270
for several months.

00:51:41.270 --> 00:51:44.410
So people inside Microsoft
and outside Microsoft,

00:51:44.410 --> 00:51:48.350
they were desperate to find
a new job. And of course,

00:51:48.350 --> 00:51:51.730
they wanted to be in the
cool thing that it's AI.

00:51:53.000 --> 00:51:57.040
So I shared with Rachel and
I shared on LinkedIn that I was

00:51:57.040 --> 00:51:58.280
so overwhelmed

00:51:58.960 --> 00:52:02.710
by the messages. And I try to

00:52:03.490 --> 00:52:07.090
reply to every message. Every
person that messages me,

00:52:07.090 --> 00:52:08.350
I try to reply.

00:52:10.060 --> 00:52:11.200
And I was like,

00:52:12.180 --> 00:52:16.050
I can't scale myself replying.
And I'm not going to do

00:52:16.830 --> 00:52:19.950
informational interviews
because I don't think it's fair

00:52:19.950 --> 00:52:21.290
for the other candidates.

00:52:22.260 --> 00:52:24.393
They all should go
through the same process.

00:52:25.120 --> 00:52:27.795
So my response was always like,

00:52:29.150 --> 00:52:30.450
please, apply.

00:52:30.450 --> 00:52:33.615
The team will review your
resume and then we can talk.

00:52:34.500 --> 00:52:37.550
I also build a FAQ,

00:52:38.430 --> 00:52:43.395
some questions that people would ask
me. Like for example, those roles,

00:52:44.100 --> 00:52:44.775
they are

00:52:45.940 --> 00:52:50.560
based here in San Francisco.
So you had to be based here.

00:52:50.560 --> 00:52:53.350
And then I explained
the reason why

00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:55.820
we were not accepting remote

00:52:57.100 --> 00:52:58.910
candidates at this point.

00:52:58.910 --> 00:53:03.440
So I took some time to do
this as well. But it was very,

00:53:03.440 --> 00:53:06.145
very, very overwhelming
because I couldn't

00:53:06.850 --> 00:53:08.560
reply to everybody.

00:53:10.192 --> 00:53:14.470
And people would get mad and
send me messages over and over

00:53:14.470 --> 00:53:17.485
and over again
trying to push for

00:53:19.432 --> 00:53:23.890
some information or to be
on the interview. And it was

00:53:23.890 --> 00:53:25.630
very stressful, I would say,

00:53:26.470 --> 00:53:28.990
being a hiring manager
in that situation.

00:53:28.990 --> 00:53:33.250
It was the first time
that this happened to that scale.

00:53:35.860 --> 00:53:36.360
- Yeah,

00:53:36.700 --> 00:53:39.610
I'd love to hear other people's
thoughts on this too if you have

00:53:40.330 --> 00:53:43.195
tips or feedback or if you want
to just put in the chat too

00:53:44.080 --> 00:53:46.370
on how you had dealt
with that before.

00:53:46.370 --> 00:53:48.310
It does sound overwhelming,

00:53:48.310 --> 00:53:51.100
and you want to be
able to respond to everybody too.

00:53:51.100 --> 00:53:53.000
- Yeah because also

00:53:53.710 --> 00:53:55.490
I've been on the
other side as well,

00:53:55.490 --> 00:54:00.250
and I would be so pissed
when the person don't reply to me.

00:54:01.510 --> 00:54:05.020
So I don't want to be that
person. But also like,

00:54:05.020 --> 00:54:06.630
how can I not burn out myself

00:54:09.310 --> 00:54:12.970
with the amount of
requests? It was insane.

00:54:12.970 --> 00:54:13.555
- Yeah.

00:54:14.830 --> 00:54:15.640
I see,

00:54:15.640 --> 00:54:19.360
there was one other Slido question that
I wanted to get to that was,

00:54:20.380 --> 00:54:23.650
do you have any advice for
people who also want to be in

00:54:23.650 --> 00:54:25.465
that advocate type role

00:54:27.010 --> 00:54:30.310
if they don't necessarily
want to be like an influencer

00:54:30.310 --> 00:54:33.550
spamming social media but want
to make good contributions to

00:54:33.550 --> 00:54:35.005
the community?

00:54:35.005 --> 00:54:38.230
- You don't have to be
that person. You don't have to go--

00:54:38.230 --> 00:54:38.440
like,

00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:41.515
there are some advocates that
they don't even have social media.

00:54:42.470 --> 00:54:45.010
So there are other things that we do.

00:54:46.120 --> 00:54:47.170
I'll give an example.

00:54:49.300 --> 00:54:53.965
Microsoft, the advocacy in
general, the advocacy role,

00:54:55.640 --> 00:54:59.090
we have three pillars.
One, it's content.

00:54:59.090 --> 00:55:01.310
So it's writing
content for example.

00:55:01.310 --> 00:55:03.730
So you don't have to be
in front of the camera or you

00:55:03.730 --> 00:55:05.440
don't have to be
on social media.

00:55:06.190 --> 00:55:07.930
The other one is
about community.

00:55:13.280 --> 00:55:15.770
It doesn't need to be an
external community but it could

00:55:15.770 --> 00:55:20.240
be a community that we
have internally. And the third

00:55:20.240 --> 00:55:22.370
pillar, it's around
product feedback.

00:55:23.090 --> 00:55:25.280
So it's very different.

00:55:25.280 --> 00:55:28.550
So I talked about three
things that people usually don't think

00:55:28.550 --> 00:55:30.620
about when they
think about advocacy,

00:55:30.620 --> 00:55:35.015
they think that you are going to
be on stage 24/7 talking to people

00:55:35.690 --> 00:55:39.440
and going to conferences all
the time, which is not true.

00:55:39.440 --> 00:55:42.890
Yes, there is a space for that.
And if you are that person,

00:55:42.890 --> 00:55:45.650
you can be that person. But also like,

00:55:45.650 --> 00:55:48.710
there are other things that you
can do as well that you don't

00:55:48.710 --> 00:55:51.530
have to be an influencer
or you don't have to be

00:55:53.150 --> 00:55:54.845
putting your face out there.

00:55:56.315 --> 00:55:57.635
- Thank you for that.

